    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809-a1">

                <pb facs="0769" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg653"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Liberian Secretary of
                            State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: By direction of His
                    Excellency the President, I have the honor to inclose herewith, for the
                    information of your Government at Washington, copies of the correspondence
                    between the Acting British Consul-General and the Liberian Secretary of State
                    touching certain recent incidents on the Anglo-Liberian frontier as reported by
                    the Government of Sierra Leone.</p>
                <p>The Liberian Government has not yet received a report from its agent on the spot,
                    but hope to communicate the same to you when it is received.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. D. B. King.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
